# TYFZA1 native FTTR service policies, loaded at controller startup.
# Up to seven services per ONU (FPGA1: one). Exact serial rows replace the
# complete wildcard set. Distinct slots execute in ascending order.
# No active rows means inventory only. Select network policy explicitly.
#
# serial: 16 hexadecimal digits in vendor-first wire order, or *
# kind: 0=Ethernet, 2=VEIP; ordinal: zero-based within that actual MIB class
# kind shared: attach all reported Ethernet and VEIP UNIs; ordinal must be 0
# shared-mcast/shared-ctc also install the original remote multicast recipe.
# With a bridge, these kinds also attach the shared native fttr-mc endpoint
# after every registered ONU is authenticated and its GEM4095 state verified.
# All multicast policies must name the same bridge (or all use - for OMCI only).
# An unselected ONU retaining GEM4095 prevents shared multicast admission.
# Factory defaults (ASIC9690/FPGA2):
# serial factory total-TCONTs bridge
# serial factory-ctc total-TCONTs bridge
# total includes management slot0; original startup uses 2, supported range2..8.
# Generates data slots1..total-1, priority0, physical DBA0/0/19440.
# total2: transparent ANI; larger totals: ANI filter100*slot, transparent UNIs.
# Last data slot owns standard multicast; factory-ctc selects the CTC recipe.
# FTTR-402 limits: first Ethernet card/all PPTP UNIs capped at4;
# first VEIP card/slot capped at1. Actual MIB card types must be present.
# A factory row replaces its entire serial/wildcard collection; it cannot mix
# with explicit rows for the same selector. Exact serial still replaces *.
# This generates the traced default recipe; it does not import saved factory
# configuration, custom bandwidth/card profiles or the FPGA1 supervisor.
# Example (choose the local bridge before enabling):
# * factory 2 br-lan
# slot: ASIC9690/FPGA2 1..7, FPGA1 1
# priority: 0..7; VID: 0..4094 for access mode, none for transparent mode,
# or filter:VID for transparent UNIs with only the ANI/GEM VLAN filter.
# The factory shared multi-service recipe uses the latter separation.
# Multiple rows for one serial must use shared/filter:VID with distinct
# slots and VIDs. At most one row owns shared-mcast/shared-ctc remote objects.
# All matching GEMs in that row's local bridge become multicast members.
# fixed/assured/maximum: hardware grant units, as in fttrctl service
# bridge: existing, up Linux bridge, or - for OMCI provisioning only
# The controller creates fttr-u<ID> for GEM ordinal1, or fttr-u<ID>-<ordinal>
# for other GEMs, with outer 802.1Q VID=GEM Port-ID.
#
# serial            kind ordinal slot priority VID  fixed assured maximum bridge
